      "text": "An effective way to parallelize this memory-bound kernel is to **tile (block)** the loop so that chunks of `x` and `y` fit entirely in the fast L1/L2 CPU cache across all `reps` repetitions. \n\nIn the original serial code, `x` and `y` (~320 MB total) are streamed from main DRAM 20 times. By processing cache-sized blocks across all repetitions before moving to the next block, memory traffic drops by a factor of 20 (reading and writing each array to DRAM only once). Furthermore, using `restrict` pointers allows the compiler to auto-vectorize the inner loop (e.g., using AVX2/FMA instructions) while preserving bit-for-bit equivalence with the serial calculation.\n\nHere is the complete modified program:\n\n```c\n/* k01_saxpy: y = a*x + y, repeated. UNIFORM cost per iteration, memory-bound. */\n#include \"common.h\"\n#include <omp.h>\n\n/* === KERNEL BEGIN === */\nstatic void kernel(long n, int reps, double a, const double *x, double *y) {\n    if (n <= 0 || reps <= 0) return;\n\n    const double * restrict rx = x;\n    double * restrict ry = y;\n    const long BLOCK = 2048;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (long i = 0; i < n; i += BLOCK) {\n        long end = (i + BLOCK < n) ? i + BLOCK : n;\n        for (int r = 0; r < reps; r++) {\n            #pragma clang loop vectorize(enable)\n            #pragma clang loop interleave(enable)\n            for (long j = i; j < end; j++) {\n                ry[j] = a * rx[j] + ry[j];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n/* === KERNEL END === */\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    long n = arg_long(argc, argv, 1, 20000000);\n    int reps = (int)arg_long(argc, argv, 2, 20);\n    double *x = xmalloc(n * sizeof *x), *y = xmalloc(n * sizeof *y);\n    rng_seed(1);\n    for (long i = 0; i < n; i++) { x[i] = rng_unit(); y[i] = rng_unit(); }\n\n    double t0 = now_sec();\n    kernel(n, reps, 0.5, x, y);\n    double t1 = now_sec();\n\n    double sum = 0.0;\n    for (long i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += y[i];\n    report(\"saxpy\", t1 - t0, sum);\n    free(x); free(y);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
